sequenceDiagram
    participant ORC as Orchestrator
    participant ADV as Adversary Agent
    participant AI as AI Provider
    participant LIB as Disruption Library
    participant SIM as Simulation Engine
    participant UI as Frontend

    Note over ORC,ADV: Adversary loop runs once per ranked plan

    ORC->>ADV: attack(plan=PlanA, world_state)
    ADV->>LIB: get_disruption_templates()
    LIB-->>ADV: DisruptionTemplate[] (port closure, demand spike, etc.)

    ADV->>AI: generate(system=adversary_prompt, user=plan+world+templates, schema=AdversaryOutputSchema)
    Note over AI: AI selects most plausible attack vectors
    AI-->>ADV: raw_findings (JSON)
    ADV->>ADV: Pydantic validate raw_findings

    loop For each finding (max 5)
        ADV->>SIM: simulate_disruption(plan=PlanA, disruption=finding.attack_vector)
        SIM-->>ADV: SimResult(failure_mode, severity, probability)
        ADV->>ADV: Record finding with sim evidence
    end

    ADV->>ADV: rate_robustness(findings) → adversary_rating
    ADV-->>ORC: AdversaryFinding[] + adversary_rating=0.71

    ORC->>ORC: Merge adversary_rating into PlanA
    ORC->>UI: plan.ranked (plans with adversary ratings)

    Note over UI: User navigates to Adversary Attack screen
    UI->>ORC: GET /api/plans/PlanA/adversary
    ORC-->>UI: AdversaryFinding[]

    Note over UI: User re-runs adversary
    UI->>ORC: POST /api/plans/PlanA/adversary/run
    ORC->>ADV: attack(plan=PlanA, world_state, force_rerun=true)
    ADV-->>ORC: new AdversaryFinding[]
    ORC->>UI: adversary.finding (via WebSocket)
